      "writtenOn": "2025-02-28T04:40:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "maybe it would make sense for the client to stop iterating once it finds one invalid chain struct? otherwise it seems like S-\u003eInvalid1-\u003eInvalid2 could translate into S-\u003eInjectedInvalidSType-\u003eInjectedInvalidSType which has multiple copies of the same chain struct. (though I\u0027m not sure whether it actually does that, and I\u0027m not sure whether multiple copies is a \"problem\" - do we validate it in the frontend?)\n\nAnd that could be chained many times, but at least I think that won\u0027t stack overflow anymore because you\u0027ve replaced the recursion with iteration?",
      "revId": "1d12cfe256f64f1fb1fe2110771236e0eca2c346",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
